                                                                        "content_type":  "text",
                                                                        "parts":  [
                                                                                      "Implemented the Flappy-style game in led_blinky.c only.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Replaced the ILI9341 demo/screensaver loop with a simple bird-and-pipes game.\n- Uses the existing ILI9341 driver over configured LPSPI0.\n- Uses SW2 through ADC0_A14 / LPADC, matching the generated pin mux.\n- Preserved BOARD_InitHardware(), SysTick LED toggling, and PWM fade behavior.\n- Game over restarts on the next SW2 press.\n\nVerification:\n- cmake --preset debug succeeded.\n- cmake --build --preset debug succeeded and linked new.elf.\n\nWarning still worth keeping in mind: GAME_SW2_PRESSED_THRESHOLD is currently 1000U; depending on the real SW2 ADC voltage levels, it may need tuning on hardware."
                                                                                  ]
                                                                    },
